id: pm-ado-ci-wrapper-child-timeout
title: Investigate linked-test wrapper retaining children after timeout
description: "During Fleet CI v2 validation, a linked command failed at the default 120-second pm watchdog while its timeout/Node descendant processes remained alive beyond that deadline. The abandoned process tree was explicitly terminated. Reproduce with synthetic fixtures, deduplicate upstream reports, and verify descendant cleanup without changing package behavior."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags[2]: ci,testing
created_at: "2026-11-15T20:39:41.927Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-16T11:00:26.335Z"
author: codex-sol
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-16T11:00:26.264Z",codex-sol,"Release-caller continuation reproduced a linked preloader command timing out at its unchanged 300-second wrapper budget on a heavily loaded shared host. Command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"relative preloads survive every installed host fixture cwd change\" test/changelog-content.test.ts. The command now correctly selects the moved regression instead of silently matching no tests. Keep this timeout separate from the release caller and source-inventory fixes; no timeout or coverage threshold was relaxed."
body: ""
